.DS_Store

# Jekyll build output - was previously tracked in this repo, which is
# not standard practice (GitHub Pages builds from source, it doesn't
# serve the committed copy) and caused a real bug: reverting stale
# tracked drift in _site/ during local dev would overwrite whatever
# `jekyll serve` had just freshly built, silently serving old content.
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.bundle/
vendor/
